{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790958562,"nonce":"H6XN1Qh1ib/L7wStSk3yzPKj3UM=","title":"a plugin's native `new` is never a constructor, so `new` on its extern class traps","message":"`NativePlugin::method_mappings` (compiler/src/compiler_plugin.rs) registers every method with `is_constructor: false`. The rpkg method table and extern-file registration (`register_extern_methods_from_typed_file`) both go through it, so `new C(...)` never finds a constructor a plugin supplies. Lowering falls back to the class's own constructor, which an extern class has no body for, and the JIT runs a trap.\n\nx-idl's Rayzor bindings declare every record and resource constructor this way:\n\n    @:native(\"window::WindowAttributes\")\n    extern class WindowAttributes {\n        @:native(\"xwindow_window_attributes_new\")\n        public function new();\n    }\n\nReproducer (xwindow's generated Rayzor surface, packed with its adapter dylib):\n\n    var attributes = new WindowAttributes();\n\n    rayzor: native crash signal=SIGILL ... in window.WindowAttributes.new [Cranelift]\n\nxgpu's generated `GpuInstance` and every descriptor record are built the same way.\n\nFix: a static method named `new` is the class's constructor; Haxe's `new` can name nothing else. With that, `new WindowAttributes()` binds to `xwindow_window_attributes_new`, and a window opens, polls events and reports its monitors under the JIT.","files":null}]}